{{also|Mund|mund'}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|mund}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*mundō||hand, protection, security}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*man-||hand}}. Cognate with German {{m|de|Mund}}, {{m|de|Munt||legal protection}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mʊnd/|/mʌnd/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} A [[hand]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} [[security]], granted by a king or earl, the violation of which was punished by a [[fine]] (a [[mundbyrd]])
# [[protection|Protection]], [[guardianship]].

===Anagrams===
* {{anagrams|en|UNDM}}

