==Albanian==

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{m|ine-pro|*mendh||to pay attention to, be vivacious}}. Compare Old Norse {{m|non|munda||aim, strive}}, Gothic {{m|got|mundon||look up}}, Old High German {{m|goh|muntar||keen, eager}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|μανθάνω||learn}}, Lithuanian {{m|lt|mañdras||alert, awake, smart, minxish}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/mʊnd/|lang=sq}}

====Noun====
{{sq-noun|g=m}}

# [[trouble]]
# [[toil]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|sq|mundur}}
* {{l|sq|mundje}}
* {{l|sq|mundim}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|sq|Muji}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|sqj-pro|sq}} {{m|sqj-pro|*māK(e)nT-}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{m|ine-pro|*magʰ-||can, to be able (to do)}}. Cognate to Lithuanian {{m|lt|mokė́ti||to be able}}, Gothic {{m|got|magan||to be able, have power}}, {{cog|cu|мошти||to be able}}. Alternatively from {{etyl|ine-pro|sq}} {{m|ine-pro|*men(s)-dʰ(e)h₂||to learn}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/mʊnd/|lang=sq}}

====Verb====
{{sq-verb|munda|mundur}}

# I [[can]].
# I am [[able]].
# I [[beat]], [[win]] over.

=====Inflection=====
{{sq-conj-c-a-ur|mund}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|sq|mundem}}

